  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gender Transformative Actions and Social Inclusion Project in Ghana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Gender Workplace Policy is aimed at ensuring Safe Spaces and ending Gender Based Violence. It aims to scale up the Draft Anti -Sexual Harassment Policy framework under the ENOUGH project across various sectors in Ghana, including private organizations, trade unions, financial institutions, academic institutions, and state agencies. With an eight -month timeframe, the project will promote policy adoption, enhance capacity through training, raise awareness through comprehensive media campaigns, and strengthen support systems for victims. The project will be implemented by Global Action for Women Empowerment (GLOWA), Songtaba, Network for Women in Growth (NEWIG), and Widows and Orphans Movement (WOM). The ultimate goal is to create safer, more equitable workplaces and reduce incidents of workplace harassment.</narrative>
  </description>
